 accepted_round;\n   320\t        self.state_cache.decided_idx = decided_idx;\n   321\t        let mut sync_txn: Vec<StorageOp<T>> = vec![\n   322\t            StorageOp::SetAcceptedRound(accepted_round),\n   323\t            StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(decided_idx),\n   324\t        ];\n   325\t        if let Some(sync) = log_sync {\n   326\t            match sync.decided_snapshot {\n   327\t                Some(SnapshotType::Complete(c)) => {\n   328\t                    self.state_cache.compacted_idx = sync.sync_idx;\n   329\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::Trim(sync.sync_idx));\n   330\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetCompactedIdx(sync.sync_idx));\n   331\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetSnapshot(Some(c)));\n   332\t                }\n   333\t                Some(SnapshotType::Delta(d)) => {\n   334\t                    let mut snapshot = self.create_decided_snapshot()?;\n   335\t                    snapshot.merge(d);\n   336\t                    self.state_cache.compacted_idx = sync.sync_idx;\n   337\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::Trim(sync.sync_idx));\n   338\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetCompactedIdx(sync.sync_idx));\n   339\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetSnapshot(Some(snapshot)));\n   340\t                }\n   341\t                None => (),\n   342\t            }\n   343\t            self.state_cache.accepted_idx = sync.sync_idx + sync.suffix.len();\n   344\t            sync_txn.push(StorageOp::AppendOnPrefix(sync.sync_idx, sync.suffix));\n   345\t            match sync.stopsign {\n   346\t                Some(ss) => {\n   347\t                    self.state_cache.stopsign = Some(ss.clone());\n   348\t                    self.state_cache.accepted_idx += 1;\n   349\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetStopsign(Some(ss)));\n   350\t                }\n   351\t                None if self.state_cache.stopsign.is_some() => {\n   352\t                    self.state_cache.stopsign = None;\n   353\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetStopsign(None));\n   354\t                }\n   355\t                None => (),\n   356\t            }\n   357\t        }\n   358\t        self.storage.write_atomically(sync_txn)?;\n   359\t        Ok(self.state_cache.accepted_idx)\n   360\t    }\n   361\t\n   362\t    fn create_decided_snapshot(&mut self) -> StorageResult<T::Snapshot> {\n   363\t        let log_decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx_without_stopsign();\n   364\t        self.create_snapshot(log_decided_idx)\n   365\t    }\n   366\t\n   367\t    pub(crate) fn create_snapshot(&self, compact_idx: usize) -> StorageResult<T::Snapshot> {\n   368\t        let current_compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n   369\t        if compact_idx < current_compacted_idx {\n   370\t            Err(CompactionErr::TrimmedIndex(current_compacted_idx))?\n   371\t        }\n   372\t        let entries = self\n   373\t            .storage\n   374\t            .get_entries(current_compacted_idx, compact_idx)?;\n   375\t        let delta = T::Snapshot::create(entries.as_slice());\n   376\t        match self.storage.get_snapshot()? {\n   377\t            Some(mut s) => {\n   378\t                s.merge(delta);\n   379\t                Ok(s)\n   380\t            }\n   381\t            None => Ok(delta),\n   382\t        }\n   383\t    }\n   384\t\n   385\t    // Creates a Delta snapshot of entries from `from_idx` to the end of the decided log and also\n   386\t    // returns the compacted idx of the created snapshot. If the range of entries contains entries\n   387\t    // which have already been compacted a valid delta cannot be created, so creates a Complete\n   388\t    // snapshot of the entire decided log instead.\n   389\t    pub(crate) fn create_diff_snapshot(\n   390\t        &self,\n   391\t        from_idx: usize,\n   392\t    ) -> StorageResult<(Option<SnapshotType<T>>, usize)> {\n   393\t        let log_decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx_without_stopsign();\n   394\t        let compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n   395\t        let snapshot = if from_idx <= compacted_idx {\n   396\t            // Some entries in range are compacted, snapshot entire decided log\n   397\t            if compacted_idx < log_decided_idx {\n   398\t                Some(SnapshotType::Complete(\n   399\t                    self.create_snapshot(log_decided_idx)?,\n   400\t                ))\n   401\t            } else {\n   402\t                // Entire decided log already snapshotted\n   403\t                self.get_snapshot()?.map(|s| SnapshotType::Complete(s))\n   404\t            }\n   405\t        } else {\n   406\t            let diff_entries = self.get_entries(from_idx, log_decided_idx)?;\n   407\t            Some(SnapshotType::Delta(T::Snapshot::create(\n   408\t                diff_entries.as_slice(),\n   409\t            )))\n   410\t        };\n    88\t    fn get_accepted_round(&self) -> StorageResult<Option<Ballot>> {\n    89\t        Ok(self.acc_round)\n    90\t    }\n    91\t\n    92\t    fn get_entries(&self, from: usize, to: usize) -> StorageResult<Vec<T>> {\n    93\t        let from = from - self.trimmed_idx;\n    94\t        let to = to - self.trimmed_idx;\n    95\t        Ok(self.log.get(from..to).unwrap_or(&[]).to_vec())\n    96\t    }\n    97\t\n    98\t    fn get_log_len(&self) -> StorageResult<usize> {\n    99\t        Ok(self.log.len())\n   100\t    }\n   101\t\n   102\t    fn get_suffix(&self, from: usize) -> StorageResult<Vec<T>> {\n   103\t        Ok(match self.log.get((from - self.trimmed_idx)..) {\n   104\t            Some(s) => s.to_vec(),\n   105\t            None => vec![],\n   106\t        })\n   107\t    }\n   108\t\n   109\t    fn get_promise(&self) -> StorageResult<Option<Ballot>> {\n   110\t        Ok(self.n_prom)\n   111\t    }\n   112\t\n   113\t    fn set_stopsign(&mut self, s: Option<StopSign>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n                .set_promise(prep.n)\n                .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n            self.state = (Role::Follower, Phase::Prepare);\n            self.current_seq_num = SequenceNumber::default();\n            let na = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_round();\n            let accepted_idx = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx();\n            let log_sync = if na > prep.n_accepted {\n                // I'm more up to date: send leader what he is missing after his decided index.\n                Some(self.create_log_sync(prep.decided_idx, prep.decided_idx))\n            } else if na == prep.n_accepted && accepted_idx > prep.accepted_idx {\n                // I'm more up to date and in same round: send leader what he is missing after his\n                // accepted index.\n                Some(self.create_log_sync(prep.accepted_idx, prep.decided_idx))\n            } else {\n                // I'm equally or less up to date\n                None\n            };\n            let promise = Promise {\n                n: prep.n,\n                n_accepted: na,\n                decided_idx: self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx(),\n                accepted_idx,\n                log_sync,\n            };\n            self.cached_promise_message = Some(promise.clone());\n            self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n                from: self.pid,\n                to: from,\n                msg: PaxosMsg::Promise(promise),\n            }));\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_acceptsync(&mut self, accsync: AcceptSync<T>, from: NodeId) {\n        if self.check_valid_ballot(accsync.n) && self.state == (Role::Follower, Phase::Prepare) {\n            self.cached_promise_message = None;\n            let new_accepted_idx = self\n                .internal_storage\n                .sync_log(accsync.n, accsync.decided_idx, Some(accsync.log_sync))\n                .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n            if self.internal_storage.get_stopsign().is_none() {\n                self.forward_buffered_proposals();\n            }\n            let accepted = Accepted {\n                n: accsync.n,\n                accepted_idx: new_accepted_idx,\n            };\n            self.state = (Role::Follower, Phase::Accept);\n            self.current_seq_num = accsync.seq_num;\n            let cached_idx = self.outgoing.len();\n            self.latest_accepted_meta = Some((accsync.n, cached_idx));\n            self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n                from: self.pid,\n                to: from,\n                msg: PaxosMsg::Accepted(accepted),\n            }));\n            #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n            self.internal_storage.set_unicache(accsync.unicache);\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn forward_buffered_proposals(&mut self) {\n        let proposals = std::mem::take(&mut self.buffered_proposals);\n        if !proposals.is_empty() {\n            self.forward_proposals(proposals);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_acceptdecide(&mut self, acc_dec: AcceptDecide<T>) {\n        if self.check_valid_ballot(acc_dec.n)\n            && self.state == (Role::Follower, Phase::Accept)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nreview={\n'action':'review','artifact_id':'81f0991cd9af429098a9e26cbda14112',\n'rationale':'Review the fixed version-1 driver and plan against raw CheckRun 4fcecc7255ae497e877cff1da4db063b and captured implementation. The observed acknowledged recovery loses an earlier decided entry from its snapshot representation.',\n'review_items':[{\n'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'no_issue_found',\n'source_ids':['M-api','M-transport','M-config','M-sequence','M-leader','M-follower','M-sync','M-memory','M-cache','M-storage-contract','M-log-contract','M-snapshot-contract','M-value-snapshot','M-sync-test'],\n'rationale': 'The fixed harness uses three fresh instances in configuration 1, pids 1/2/3, batch_size=1, actual MemoryStorage, and public try_become_leader/append/message/reconnected APIs. It constructs no Paxos messages and changes no stored protocol state. Its queue preserves emission order for each connected pair. The partition discards every message involving node 3 independently of type or outcome; raw output records loss of AcceptDecide(Item(22)) and Decide(2). The first prefix is checked on all three nodes as decided [11]; after the partition, nodes 1 and 2 are checked as decided [11,22], while node 3 remains accepted=decided=1 with [11]. Restoring transport precedes the documented reconnected(1) call. Target-produced Promise carries old boundary 1, and target-produced AcceptSync carries Delta [22], decided=sync_idx=2, matching ballot (config=1,n=1,pid=1), session=2,counter=1. The source path reconnected -> Recover -> equal-ballot Prepare -> Follower/Prepare -> matching-ballot AcceptSync is legal. No timer expiry, crash, pending batch or competing leadership is needed for this finite safety history. The implementation completes synchronously and emits Accepted at index 2 before observation. The completed flag is derived from that actual reply and the public Accept-phase report, not assumed readiness. The result records accepted=decided=compacted=2 and public read Some([Snapshotted(... Prefix([22]))]). Exclusive single-thread ownership ensures reads describe one live post-handler state; no shutdown or cached application copy intervenes. Identity case/receiver/sync_id is independent of compared contents; prefix and sync prerequisites precede the unique result and admission_alias selects sync. The expected string [11,22] comes from a prior actual leader read corroborated by node 2 and explicit proposal checks. The assertion compares all ordered contents, not only length or last value. Snapshot::create clones its input contents and merge concatenates changes, matching M-value-snapshot; M-log-contract requires decided entries not be reverted and M-snapshot-contract requires preservation through snapshots. Thus [22] versus [11,22] is a complete local counterexample to C-delta-prefix, not simply a changed metadata value. Source reconstruction explains it: sync_log assigns decided_idx=2 before create_decided_snapshot; that calls get_entries(0,2) on the receiver log of length 1. MemoryStorage returns empty for this incomplete interval, as required by Storage. The resulting empty snapshot is merged with Delta [22] and stored at compacted boundary 2. This causal explanation is source-derived; internal intermediate reads were not instrumented. The observed result itself establishes the content loss. Cargo test success only means the setup and driver completed; the controller comparison independently records violated with no parse errors.',\n'counterevidence':['Complete snapshots bypass local Delta base reconstruction and are not contradicted by this witness.','The repository ValueSnapshot equality compares only latest_value; a passing latest-value test would be consistent with observed [22] and does not rebut loss of 11.','Ballot, phase and sequence recovery guards are satisfied and protect against stale traffic; they do not validate Delta content alignment.'],\n'limitations':['Single follower reconnect witness; leader-side synchronization, an already accepted but undecided suffix, and a previously compacted receiver were not executed.','No production application endpoint or durable process-crash recovery was tested; the violation is the publicly readable decided snapshot representation.','Actual selected-test compilation enabled default/macros/omnipaxos_macros/serde; metadata-listed async_runtime and logging were not active in this execution.','The historical plan uncertainty about pending compilation/execution is superseded by the retained completed CheckRun; no fixed artifact bytes were changed.'],\n'report_title':'增量快照恢复丢失已决定的前缀',\n'report_answer':'可信执行中，节点 3 原已决定 [11]，重连后收到增量 [22] 并确认恢复至索引 2，但公开读取仅返回快照 [22]，应有内容为 [11,22]。固定驱动使用真实协议消息及合法断连重连流程；该结论限于已执行的内存存储、单配置恢复场景。'\n}],\n'feedback':{'ref_ids':['4fcecc7255ae497e877cff1da4db063b','81f0991cd9af429098a9e26cbda14112','f628591758414257938b7e7c8d4e0615','B-sync','F-snapshot','M-sync','M-memory'],\n'answered':'The fixed recovery history reaches acknowledged Delta synchronization and loses previously decided content: expected [11,22], observed snapshot [22] at compacted/decided index 2. Source tracing identifies premature decided-boundary assignment followed by an incomplete local read returning empty. This answers the candidate missing-interval discriminator without establishing all possible Delta histories.',\n'remaining':['Independent unread configuration-isolation and async-runtime responsibilities remain in the frontier; no rerun of this same missing-interval case is needed.'],\n'understanding':'updated','rationale':'Preserve the actual counterexample, legal-history account and current correspondence review for the executed version. Wider variants are limits, not prerequisites for this local counterexample.'}\n}\nopen('snapshot_review.json','w').write(json.dumps(review,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_review.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_11-40-15-omnipaxos-real-run --submission snapshot_review.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
